-- A member has a name and an email, and no two members share an email. `velle compare` from
-- `46-unique-field-contention-line-before.velle`, the member without its email, to this file
-- prints:
--
--   ## What was edited
--
--   - Member now has the field email (a text, no two the same).
--     In the spec: 46-unique-field-contention-line-accepted.velle, line 22, `act Member`
--
--   ## What that changes
--   ...
--   ### Member
--
--   - A new Member now waits its turn behind other work on the same email value. Before: behind nothing.
--     In the spec: 46-unique-field-contention-line-accepted.velle, line 22, `act Member`
--
-- `velle compare` from an empty spec (an empty file) to this file prints only "New: Member, a
-- request someone makes, kept as a record, with name (a text), email (a text, no two the
-- same).", and no section "What that changes". The two reports end at the same spec and disagree
-- on whether a new Member waits behind other work on the same email, so a report over a whole
-- session drops what the report over one change said.
act Member {
    name: text
    email: text unique
}
